{"audit": {"coverageKind": "diagnoses", "state": "unaudited"}, "id": "2021_parsley:0/children/0/children/0:diagnosis", "kind": "diagnosis", "notes": "\"This is not a comprehensive listing of the probable orders to be\nincluded in this sub class and those listed below and includes only\nthose whose representatives were part of this study.\"\n", "path": "0/children/0/children/0", "printedAttribution": "as-record", "source": "2021_parsley", "subject": "gogiida-subclass", "text": "Gogiids with a non-pored, early juvenile stage of mostly hexagonal\nplates followed by circular to ovoid epispires, or paedomorphically,\nin later stages limits epispires to juvenile-like circular epispires\nor retains the early juvenile non-pored stage throughout ontogeny.\nYounger (Upper Cambrian to Ordovician) forms modify radiating (plate\ncenter to plate angles), reinforcing ridges into hollowed folds that\nappear to be, in addition to reinforcing structures, to respiratory\nstructures (Middle to Upper Ordovician). Ambulacral pattern 2-1-2\nnever attaining true pentameral symmetry. Stems/stalks evolve from\nbeing irregularly plated (Lower and Middle Cambrian) to primarily\nholomerous (Middle Cambrian to Upper Ordovician).\n", "tree": "taxonomy"}
